Cell["\<\
Where we have the boundary variables and their time derivative obtained by \
solving the equation fed with the asymptotic expansions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.909585034673765*^9, 
  3.909585086002244*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8dbf2cb7-77f1-4187-80fb-\
2cf0a31acbf5"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gauge: compute_gauge_t and equation_outer_coefficient", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9089512630287943`*^9, 3.908951277095985*^9}, {
  3.908951327803493*^9, 3.908951328737679*^9}, {3.9089513598827677`*^9, 
  3.908951365944531*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ab0ec347-1d33-4aaa-a458-\
72f59f3dc7b8"],

Cell["\<\
We want to find the coefficient for the xi time derivative equation. We will \
put these, after being translated to Julia language and simplified through \
Simpy, in the file equation_outer_coefficient, in the function xi_t_eq_coeff, \
that is called in the file compute_gauge_t.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9089513701975727`*^9, 
  3.90895145399369*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"afca6571-ac91-47af-8bff-\
dc71168b749f"],

Cell["\<\
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s take the Theta equation. Then we rewrite the spatial \
derivatives for all the variables except for xi (they have to be explicit). 
Then we collect the time derivative of xi mixed with the other derivatives. \
The equation should have the form:
(azz Dzz + ayy Dyy + Azy Dzy + bz Dz + by Dy + c Id) xi_t = -S\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9095685430888863`*^9, 3.90956856515408*^9}, {
  3.909568840829561*^9, 3.9095689410773153`*^9}, {3.909569319671631*^9, 
  3.9095693304418783`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0d738ce8-a819-48da-b824-\
eb6082d3821f"],

